    notes: 'Phosphate salt of the vibriostatic agent O/129. CHEBI:73908 2,4-diamino-6,7-diisopropylpteridine
      is the free base; CHEBI has no term for the phosphate salt, so Section 3 applies:
      registry identifier plus narrowMatch to the parent rather than asserting the
      salt IS the free base. The Vibriostat and Vibriostatic Agent O/129 residual
      labels are the free base and were mapped to CHEBI:73908 separately (#213).'
